			)
		)
		(uuid "29133d3d-9f10-4b99-8075-c5475b7b75c8")
	)
	(text "GPIO0 (J3-13) as plain GPIO: add to config.txt\n  force_eeprom_read=0\n  disable_poe_fan=1\nor the firmware probes GPIO0/1 (I2C0) for a HAT EEPROM at boot."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 60.96 113.792 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2febd577-31f7-469f-ba33-988b303c7ae1")
	)
	(text "EEPROM WRITE PROTECT (EEPROM_nWP, J5 3-4)\nThe CM5 pulls EEPROM_nWP up internally (100k), so the\nbootloader EEPROM is writable unless J5 3-4 is fitted.\nThe jumper only takes effect once protection is enabled\nin the bootloader config (CM5 datasheet 2.12.2).\n\nProduction:\n- Set eeprom_write_protect=1 in the bootloader config\n  (via usbboot or rpi-eeprom-config) before shipping.\n- Fit the J5 3-4 jumper. The EEPROM is then protected\n  from power-up (CM5 datasheet 3.1).\n\nBootloader update:\n- Remove J5 3-4, update via usbboot or self-update,\n  then refit the jumper.\n\nWhy not a GPIO with a pull-down: CM5 EEPROM updates run\nonly via usbboot or bootloader self-update, before Linux can drive a GPIO, so the pin could\nnever be released for an update."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.646 96.012 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "342137f9-6d01-4fc1-9444-f251dee01ff6")
	)
	(text "H6: optional I2C1 pull-ups R12/R13, normally OPEN.\nCM5 already pulls GPIO2/3 up with 1.8k (CM5 datasheet Table 4).\nFit H6 only for a long, high-capacitance bus\nat 400 kHz: ~1k total, ~2.9 mA sink at 0.4 V\n(I2C spec min 3 mA, so compliant devices are OK)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 120.65 187.452 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "372d484b-1e6c-47c1-8198-246722d57e13")
	)
	(text "I2C PULL-UPS\nI2C1: GPIO2 = I2C1_SDA (J3-24), GPIO3 = I2C1_SCL (J3-22)\nPulled up to 3.3 V (GPIO_VREF) by 1.8 kΩ inside the CM5\n(CM5 datasheet Table 4, pins 56/58). No board pull-ups\nare needed. R12/R13 (2.2k, fitted via H6) are optional."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.98 129.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "46118630-decc-4935-a2a7-ab48bf33e440")
	)
	(text "EEPROM write protect = Jumper Pins 3-4\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 227.838 59.182 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify right bottom)
		)
		(uuid "47812c5e-b3cf-46a9-8acb-f25fa89ea43d")
	)
	(text "GPIO3"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 109.982 84.074 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "49c52580-cdce-44c0-b079-b639903359fb")
	)
	(text "CONSOLE UART (J4): CM5 UART0, 3.3 V logic, 115200 baud, 8N1, no flow control\n  J4-1  BOOT_CONSOLE_RXD (GPIO15, CM5 receives)   <- adapter TXD\n  J4-2  BOOT_CONSOLE_TXD (GPIO14, CM5 transmits)  -> adapter RXD\n  J4-3  GND                                       -- adapter GND\nTX and RX cross over: the adapter TXD goes to the CM5 RXD.\n\nUse an inexpensive USB-to-TTL serial cable (PL2303 / CP2102 / FTDI type) with\nfemale jumper leads. Typical colours: black GND, white RXD, green TXD, red 5V.\nCheck the labels on your cable.\n\nDO NOT connect the adapter 5V lead. The board powers itself and J4 has no 5V pin.\nA loose 5V lead can short to the header or the board, so it is best to cut it off\n(or insulate it).\nUse an adapter with 3.3 V signals only. CM5 GPIOs are not 5 V tolerant: check that\nthe adapter TXD idles at about 3.3 V with a meter before connecting.\n\nLinux console on GPIO14/15: dtparam=uart0_console in config.txt (Pi 5 / CM5 kernels).\nEarly bootloader messages go to the module debug UART, not to these pins.\nTO CHECK on first boards against the current Raspberry Pi documentation."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 147.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "59b5c7cd-9338-40a3-9b53-036619d169b0")
	)
	(text "J3 pins 2 and 4 are GND.\nOn the CM4 board they were the AIN0/AIN1 ADC inputs.\nThe CM5 has no ADC pins (module pins 94/96 are now\nCC1/CC2), so the inputs and their clamps are removed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 60.452 110.744 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6117e5ac-d521-40e8-b2d3-ce9f741e644f")
	)
	(text "CM5 External Header Pins"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18.288 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 5.08 5.08)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "642d486b-cf79-4856-b083-3b50ef9873a1")
	)
